> magic-resistant, apparently.
>
> Is there any way to reclaim my pet?  (Other than polying it into
> something else, charming it, and then trying to poly back!  Unlikely.)

Well, technically an arch-lich has a base magic resistance of 90 (out
of 100) - so it's not completely immune to charming. But your chances
are highly unlikely. In addition, your chance to successfully charm the
monster is based on your XL and the monster's XL - most likely the lich
is higher level than you and this makes it even harder for you to charm
it. I'm assuming you're using the spell "charm monster" and can cast it
repeatedly.

Polying the lich will still be difficult because of the 90 MR - but
shouldn't take terribly long. I'm assuming you're using a poly trap,
and i think the XL ratio doesn't come into effect in that case - it
should be a straight 10% shot of polymorphing every time he steps on
the trap. I could be wrong, however.



